      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FIRST CHORUS (5) is flying, a winner of her past three. She's stepped up and down slightly in trip all campaign but it hasn't mattered, backed off the map and doing enough at Caulfield Heath last time. Back to 1500m now, she gets in light again and the outstanding placement from the camp can net her another win. JUSTADEEL (6) ran well fresh in Sydney and is right up to these down in the weights. REGAL ZEUS (1) didn't fire in two runs in Queensland but is a tough horse to catch when right. ST LAWRENCE (8) finds a more suitable race this time around. He's been freshened since a plain run here last time out and an improved run is on the cards.",
